# Project Tracking

## Purpose
This file is the single source of truth for codebase-level changes in this repository.

## Update Policy
- Append a new log entry whenever the assistant changes the codebase.
- Include date, branch, changed files, reason, impact, and verification.
- Keep entries chronological (newest first).
- Use the template below for consistency.

## Entry Template
### YYYY-MM-DD | Branch: <branch-name> | Change: <short-title>
- Type: Feature | Fix | Refactor | Docs | Test | Infra
- Summary: <what changed>
- Files: <comma-separated file list>
- Why: <reason>
- Impact: <behavioral impact>
- Verification: <tests/checks run>
- Notes: <optional>

## Change Log
### 2026-04-24 | Branch: harish | Change: Add deterministic WhatsApp post-launch messaging flow
- Type: Fix
- Summary: Added task-intent parsing for WhatsApp message target/content and deterministic post-launch actions to search contact, open chat, type message, and send.
- Files: hawk/agent.py, tests/test_agent.py, Project Tracking
- Why: The workflow opened WhatsApp but often stopped before sending the message for prompts like "send message to <contact>, message content(<text>)".
- Impact: WhatsApp launch tasks with explicit recipient and message content now continue through contact selection and message submission with a predictable action sequence.
- Verification: Added parser/planner unit tests and ran full test suite with venv Python (22 passed).
- Notes: Sequence uses Ctrl+F search in WhatsApp desktop and ends with Enter to send.

### 2026-04-24 | Branch: harish | Change: Add detailed model workflow documentation
- Type: Docs
- Summary: Added a dedicated end-to-end workflow document explaining startup, task input handling, snapshot/diff structuring, model interaction, intent parsing, execution, verifier flow, and stop conditions.
- Files: HAWK_Model_Workflow_Detailed.md, Project Tracking
- Why: User requested detailed documentation describing exactly how the model pipeline works from start to finish.
